---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Home" description="I study how AI systems communicate reliability, uncertainty, and numerical precision—and how these signals shape human reliance and decision quality" ogImage="/og/home.png" hideTopBar>

<!-- ================================================================ -->
<!-- Hybrid editorial homepage: identity rail + research agenda flow   -->
<!-- ================================================================ -->
<div class="container-shell">
  <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-0 lg:gap-16">

    <!-- ============================================================ -->
    <!-- LEFT — identity rail (sticky on lg+, stacks first on mobile)   -->
    <!-- ============================================================ -->
    <div class="w-full lg:w-[380px] lg:min-w-[380px] lg:sticky lg:top-16 lg:self-start py-10 lg:py-16">

      <p class="rail-kicker mb-3">Human-Centered AI · AI Evaluation · Human Decision-Making</p>
      <p class="rail-name mb-1">Baixin Guo</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-[0.7rem] text-[var(--color-text-muted)] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] mb-5">Max · independent researcher</p>

      <h1 class="mb-5">
        Human–AI decision-making under uncertainty
      </h1>

      <p class="font-sans text-[0.95rem] text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-4">
        I study how AI systems communicate reliability, uncertainty, and numerical precision — and how these signals shape human reliance and decision quality.
      </p>
      <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Current work: CheckMyCoach human validation toward the combined Precision Illusion + CheckMyCoach paper — no human-participant findings are claimed.
      </p>

      <!-- Identity links -->
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 mb-8 font-mono text-[0.75rem]">
        <a href="https://github.com/GBX-Max1220" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[var(--color-primary)] hover:text-[var(--color-primary-dim)] transition-colors">GitHub</a>
        <a href="/cv/" class="text-[var(--color-primary)] hover:text-[var(--color-primary-dim)] transition-colors">CV</a>
        <a href="mailto:gbx1220max@gmail.com" class="text-[var(--color-primary)] hover:text-[var(--color-primary-dim)] transition-colors">Email</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/baixin-guo-681113285/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)] transition-colors">LinkedIn</a>
      </div>

      <!-- Editorial visual (conceptual orientation, not a banner) -->
      <figure class="hidden sm:block mb-8">
        <img src={'/images/home-hero.png'} alt="Conceptual overview of human–AI decision calibration research" width="1200" height="500" loading="lazy" class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-rule-light)]" />
      </figure>

      <a href="#research" class="link-arrow">Explore the research program ↓</a>
    </div>

    <!-- ============================================================ -->
    <!-- RIGHT — research agenda flow                                  -->
    <!-- ============================================================ -->
    <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 py-10 lg:py-16">

      <!-- RESEARCH PROGRAM (editorial argument) -->
      <section id="research" class="mb-14">
        <span class="section-kicker">Research program</span>
        <h2 class="mt-2 mb-2">One agenda: diagnose → build → adapt</h2>
        <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-6 max-w-2xl">
          How people mis-rely on AI advice, how to measure and correct that reliance, and how systems might adapt — one agenda across measurement, intervention, and simulation.
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-0">
          <!-- 01 Diagnose -->
          <div class="arc-item">
            <span class="arc-index">01 · Diagnose</span>
            <p class="arc-question mt-1 mb-2">How and why do people mis-rely on AI outputs?</p>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-3">
              The Precision-Illusion taxonomy and FitCalib-Bench are historical measurement work behind this question — how unsupported numerical precision shapes reliance. <span class="work-kind">Historical method</span>
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
              <a href="/research/measuring-ai-reliability/fitcalib-bench/" class="link-arrow">FitCalib-Bench audit →</a>
              <a href="/blog/precision-illusion-intro/" class="link-arrow">Precision Illusion taxonomy →</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- 02 Build -->
          <div class="arc-item">
            <span class="arc-index">02 · Build</span>
            <p class="arc-question mt-1 mb-2">Can systems improve appropriate reliance?</p>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-3">
              CheckMyCoach is the current empirical thread — an intervention prototype with a documented offline 40-case run, with human validation as the active step. InteractionKit is the released measurement infrastructure it builds on. <span class="work-kind">Current work · released</span>
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
              <a href="/research/building-trustworthy-ai/checkmycoach/" class="link-arrow">CheckMyCoach →</a>
              <a href="/research/building-trustworthy-ai/interactionkit/" class="link-arrow">InteractionKit →</a>
              <a href="/research/building-trustworthy-ai/interactionkit/research-brief/" class="link-arrow">Research brief →</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- 03 Adapt -->
          <div class="arc-item">
            <span class="arc-index">03 · Adapt</span>
            <p class="arc-question mt-1 mb-2">Can AI respond to individual trust context?</p>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-3">
              CalTrust explores bandit-style adaptation in simulation only — reported proxy metrics describe the simulator, not human trust. <span class="work-kind">Simulation only</span>
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
              <a href="/research/understanding-human-trust/caltrust/" class="link-arrow">CalTrust →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SELECTED WORK -->
      <section id="work" class="mb-14">
        <span class="section-kicker">Selected work</span>
        <h2 class="mt-2 mb-5">Three threads, one agenda</h2>

        <div class="space-y-5">
          <article class="card-static">
            <h3 class="text-[1.1rem] mb-1.5">CheckMyCoach</h3>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-2">
              A four-module intervention prototype that routes AI-advice cases, generates candidate revisions, and runs deterministic surface checks. It is the current empirical thread — human validation of uncertainty communication is the active research step.
            </p>
            <p class="work-kind mb-2">Intervention prototype · current work</p>
            <a href="/research/building-trustworthy-ai/checkmycoach/" class="link-arrow">CheckMyCoach →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="card-static">
            <h3 class="text-[1.1rem] mb-1.5">InteractionKit</h3>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-2">
              Typed experiment infrastructure — JSON Schema and structured event logging — for reproducible AI-interaction experiments. v1.0.0 is released and software-verified.
            </p>
            <p class="work-kind mb-2">Measurement infrastructure · released</p>
            <a href="/research/building-trustworthy-ai/interactionkit/" class="link-arrow">InteractionKit →</a>
          </article>

          <article class="card-static">
            <h3 class="text-[1.1rem] mb-1.5">Knowledge Compiler</h3>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-2">
              A provenance-recovered corpus and pipeline for structured knowledge from domain textbooks — 2,305 files, 2,294 unique IDs. It is a corpus artifact; no validity claim is made.
            </p>
            <p class="work-kind mb-2">Corpus &amp; pipeline · historical</p>
            <a href="/research/building-trustworthy-ai/knowledge-compiler/" class="link-arrow">Knowledge Compiler →</a>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-5">
          <a href="/research/" class="link-arrow">View all research →</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- LATEST -->
      <section id="latest">
        <div class="flex items-end justify-between mb-4">
          <div>
            <span class="section-kicker">Latest</span>
            <h2 class="mt-2">Activity</h2>
          </div>
          <a href="/blog/" class="link-arrow">More →</a>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-[var(--color-surface)] rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-rule-light)] px-5 py-2">
          <div class="log-item">
            <span class="log-date">Jul 31</span>
            <div class="log-dot"></div>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)]">InteractionKit v1.0.0 released — 7 contract tests, type checking, production build, and clean-install reproduction</p>
            <span class="log-cat">Release</span>
          </div>
          <div class="log-item">
            <span class="log-date">Jul 11</span>
            <div class="log-dot"></div>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)]"><a href="/demo/checkmycoach/" class="link-arrow">CheckMyCoach Interactive Demo</a> live — M1–M4 pipeline visualization</p>
            <span class="log-cat">Release</span>
          </div>
          <div class="log-item">
            <span class="log-date">Jul 3</span>
            <div class="log-dot"></div>
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)]">Expanded discussion with a dual-process theory framing</p>
            <span class="log-cat">Writing</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>

  </div>
</div>

</BaseLayout>
